BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fujifilm-gfx-challenge-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: FUJIFILM GFX Challenge Grant Program 2026
DESCRIPTION:The GFX Challenge Grant Program\, sponsored by FUJIFILM and run
 ning since 2021\, awards 5 Global Grant Awards (USD 10\,000) and 10 Region
 al Grant Awards (USD 5\,000) to help aspiring creatives bring imaging proj
 ects to life. It is designed to nurture emerging and promising content cre
 ators\, giving them the opportunity to create content on topics with signi
 ficant meaning to them while gaining experience with FUJIFILM GFX System g
 ear\, including the GFX ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera. Proposed projects may
  be submitted as still photography or in movie format. AWARDS: both tiers 
 include complimentary use of a GFX System camera body and two GF lenses fo
 r the duration of the project\, plus mentoring and technical assistance fr
 om Fujifilm technicians and product experts. At the end of the production 
 period in May 2027\, recipients' final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.
 com\, with a series of exhibitions planned in various countries. ELIGIBILI
 TY: open to both amateur and professional photographers and videographers 
 who are residents of the countries/regions listed in the Entry Submission 
 section of the program page\; not open to employees or officers of FUJIFIL
 M and its subsidiaries. TO APPLY: combine three items into a single PDF: (
 1) the preformatted cover letter (downloadable from the program page)\; (2
 ) the project proposal covering descriptive plan\, objectives\, evaluation
  and outcome measures\, communications\, how you will use the Fujifilm par
 tnership and mentoring\, schedule\, and budget\; (3) a portfolio for each 
 individual involved. Proposals must be in English (optionally accompanied 
 by a version in your own language\; language proficiency is not judged). E
 ntry period 16 June to 17 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: FUJIFILM\nLocation
 : Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Submission
  on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus plann
 ed exhibitions in various countries.\nAward: 5 Global Grant Awards of USD 
 10\,000 and 10 Regional Grant Awards of USD 5\,000. All recipients also ge
 t complimentary use of a GFX System camera body (including the FUJIFILM GF
 X ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera) and two GF lenses for the duration of the p
 roject\, plus mentoring and technical assistance from Fujifilm technicians
  and product experts. Total approximate retail value of all awards: USD 22
 9\,500. No purchase necessary\; no entry fee.\nDuration: Application windo
 w 16 June to 17 August 2026. Production period concludes in May 2027\, aft
 er which final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.com and in a planned ser
 ies of exhibitions.\n\nMore: https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challen
 ge-grant-program/year-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challenge-grant-program/year-2026
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Subm
 ission on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus
  planned exhibitions in various countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:institut-francais-cite-internationale-des-arts-2027-2028@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Deadline: Institut francais x Cite internationale des arts Residenc
 ies 2027-2028
DESCRIPTION:Residency programme run by the Institut francais de Paris with 
 the Cite internationale des arts\, one of France's largest international a
 rtist mobility programmes\, supporting nearly seventy artists and cultural
  professionals each year. It offers furnished individual live-work studios
  in the Marais for 3\, 6 or 9 months across four quarterly windows between
  April 2027 and April 2028 (arrivals 9 April 2027\, 9 July 2027\, 8 Octobe
 r 2027\, or 7 January 2028)\, plus access to an auditorium\, exhibition sp
 aces\, rehearsal studios and shared printmaking\, screen-printing and cera
 mics workshops. The Institut francais covers the monthly cost of the studi
 o\; the artist's nominating partner organisation submits the application a
 nd must provide a stipend of at least EUR 1\,100 per month plus internatio
 nal travel\, insurance and visa fees. ELIGIBILITY: established artists and
  cultural professionals of any nationality who have lived outside France f
 or at least 5 years\, with an active professional practice\, a clearly def
 ined research or creative project\, and professional-level French and/or E
 nglish\; open across disciplines (theatre\, dance\, performance\, visual a
 rts\, music\, literature\, cinema\, architecture\, design\, digital creati
 on\, photography\, fashion\, crafts\, curating\, and more). IMPORTANT: art
 ists cannot apply directly - a partner organisation (French cultural netwo
 rk abroad\, or a French or foreign cultural organisation) must nominate an
 d support the applicant\, committing financial and professional support be
 fore\, during and after the residency. Applications open 1 July 2026\; fre
 e to apply. Deadline: 8 October 2026\, 11:59 PM CET.\n\nOrganisation: Inst
 itut francais de Paris (with Cite internationale des arts)\nLocation: Pari
 s\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Marais\, 18 rue de l'Hotel de V
 ille\, 4th arrondissement)\nAward: Furnished\, Wi-Fi-equipped studio apart
 ment in Paris with monthly costs covered by the Institut francais. The nom
 inating partner organisation must provide a residency stipend of at least 
 EUR 1\,100 per month and cover the artist's international travel\, insuran
 ce (health\, repatriation\, liability) and any visa fees. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: 3\, 6\, or 9 months (1 to 3 consecutive quarters) between A
 pril 2027 and April 2028\n\nMore: https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/prog
 ramme/residence-and-professional-mobility/residencies-institut-francais-x-
 cite-internationale?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/programme/residence-and-professiona
 l-mobility/residencies-institut-francais-x-cite-internationale?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Marais\, 18 rue de 
 l'Hotel de Ville\, 4th arrondissement)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:legalization-project-immigrant-content-creators-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Legalization Project: Immigrant Content Creators Prog
 ram 2026-27
DESCRIPTION:The Legalization Project is running a nine-month programme for 
 experienced content creators who want to make engaging\, accessible work a
 bout U.S. immigration law\, policy and the issues affecting immigrant comm
 unities. Rather than commissioning one-off pieces\, it pairs a USD 10\,000
  stipend with actual legal grounding: training in U.S. immigration law and
  policy\, ongoing updates from immigration attorneys and advocates\, and c
 ontinuous feedback on the content you make. This suits creators already wo
 rking in video\, social or short-form documentary who want to report accur
 ately on a fast-moving legal area rather than guess at it. ELIGIBILITY: ex
 perienced content creators who are immigrants. The programme is explicitly
  open to immigrants of ALL statuses. APPLICATION: preliminary applications
  are due 17 August 2026\, through the programme page at legalizationprojec
 t.notion.site/icc-program (also circulated as bit.ly/icc-program). Being a
  preliminary application\, expect a second stage after this date.\n\nOrgan
 isation: The Legalization Project\nLocation: United States focus (content 
 covers U.S. immigration law and policy). Programme delivery format not spe
 cified in the call.\nAward: USD 10\,000 stipend\, plus training in U.S. im
 migration law and policy\, regular updates from immigration attorneys and 
 advocates\, and ongoing feedback and support on your content. No applicati
 on fee.\nDuration: Nine months\n\nMore: https://legalizationproject.notion
 .site/icc-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://legalizationproject.notion.site/icc-program?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States focus (content covers U.S. immigration law and polic
 y). Programme delivery format not specified in the call.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:liveline-fund-round-1-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260819
SUMMARY:Deadline: Liveline Fund: Round 1 (UK grassroots live music)
DESCRIPTION:Liveline is a national risk-sharing fund rebuilding grassroots 
 touring\, programming and local music scenes across the UK\, delivered by 
 Music Venue Trust with Save Our Scene and the Association of Independent P
 romoters\, alongside the LIVE Trust and the industry's voluntary levy on s
 tadium and arena tickets. The premise is that good shows are not happening
  because the downside risk is too high\, so rather than a traditional subs
 idy it is an incentive-led model that only pays out when things go wrong. 
 FOUR FUNDS: (1) GUARANTORSHIP SCHEME covers up to 80 percent of losses on 
 an individual show or tour\, for promoters\, in-house bookers\, artists or
  their representatives\; break even and nothing is paid\, turn a profit an
 d you keep it. (2) LOCAL SCENE DEVELOPMENT FUND covers venue hire costs an
 d local promoter training to build regular programming\, for independent p
 romoters or venues developing an in-house programme. (3) TOUR EXTENSION AN
 D REGIONAL ACCESS FUND covers the long travel\, fuel\, accommodation and f
 erry costs that stop tours reaching remote parts of the UK\, for promoters
 \, agents\, management and artists. (4) GENRE SPECIFIC SAFETY AND ACCESS F
 UND covers extra security\, licensing and structural costs for genres and 
 scenes that face additional barriers\, for venues\, promoters\, artists or
  collectives. ELIGIBILITY: grassroots venues (Music Venue Alliance member 
 venues)\, independent promoters including AIP members\, in-house venue pro
 grammers\, and artists\, agents and teams building sustainable tours. Guar
 antorship shows must be at MVA subscribed venues\, and for a full tour at 
 least 70 percent of dates must be at subscribed MVT venues. TWO CATCHES WO
 RTH KNOWING: tours must NOT already be announced\, and Liveline funds a he
 adline artist only once. Applications for Round 1 close Tuesday 18 August 
 2026. Start with the eligibility checker at livelinefund.uk\, or contact i
 nfo@livelinefund.uk.\n\nOrganisation: Liveline\, delivered by Music Venue 
 Trust with Save Our Scene and the Association of Independent Promoters\nLo
 cation: United Kingdom. Guarantorship shows must be at Music Venue Allianc
 e member venues\; for a full tour at least 70 percent of dates must be at 
 subscribed MVT venues. Regional focus includes the Highlands and Islands\,
  West Wales and Northern Ireland.\nAward: No fixed grant sizes published\;
  every application is assessed case by case against a real budget rather t
 han first come first served. The Guarantorship Scheme covers up to 80 perc
 ent of losses on a show or tour: if it breaks even nothing is paid\, and i
 f it turns a profit the promoter or venue keeps it. The other three funds 
 cover venue hire\, travel\, accommodation\, ferry and remote-access costs\
 , or genre-specific safety\, licensing and access costs. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Round 1\; applications close Tuesday 18 August 2026\n\nMore:
  https://livelinefund.uk/funding-overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://livelinefund.uk/funding-overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United Kingdom. Guarantorship shows must be at Music Venue Allianc
 e member venues\; for a full tour at least 70 percent of dates must be at 
 subscribed MVT venues. Regional focus includes the Highlands and Islands\,
  West Wales and Northern Ireland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-england-music-growth-fund-small-strand-2026@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260829T072942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council England: Music Growth Fund\, GBP 1\,000-40\,
 000 strand
DESCRIPTION:The Music Growth Fund is Arts Council England's new investment 
 programme for growth in new music\, meaning original live performance\, so
 und recording or musical work recently or newly created or performed by li
 ving UK-based artists and music creators. It sits inside the wider GBP 45 
 million Music Growth Package. WHO IT IS FOR: music festivals\, music manag
 ers\, music promoters\, music publishers\, record labels\, recording studi
 os\, rehearsal spaces and grassroots music venues\, plus established secto
 r bodies and other sector support organisations that support them. Each ap
 plicant type has its own Applicant Specific Guidance on the Music Growth P
 ackage pages. IMPORTANT: this is business and organisational investment\, 
 not a grant for individual artists to make work. Individual artists\, band
 s\, producers and artist collectives should instead look at the separate M
 usic Creators Growth Fund (GBP 10\,000-20\,000)\, whose guidance lands 1 S
 eptember 2026 with the portal opening 1 October 2026. WHAT TO PROPOSE: how
  investment will be used to grow music businesses and/or the wider music i
 ndustry\, and enhance opportunities for artists and music creators\, indus
 try professionals\, music fans and new audiences. Growth can mean increase
 d reach\, stronger business models\, improved sustainability\, skills deve
 lopment or expanded capacity\, and is judged in the context of each applic
 ant's own scale and ambitions. DECISION CRITERIA: potential for growth\, e
 ffective use of funds\, contribution to a fairer and more inclusive music 
 industry\, and contribution to a climate resilient music industry. BEFORE 
 YOU START: you need an approved profile on the Arts Council grants managem
 ent system before you can submit\, so allow time for that. Arts Council re
 serves the right to change the programme\, so check you are on the latest 
 guidance. THIS STRAND: GBP 1\,000 to GBP 40\,000\, with a GBP 3\,000\,000 
 annual budget for 2026/27 and a 25 percent cash match requirement. ROUNDS 
 FOR 2026/27 (GBP 1\,000-40\,000 strand): Round 1 opens 6 August and closes
  3 September 2026\, decision 28 October. Round 2 opens 4 September and clo
 ses 15 October 2026\, decision 28 October. Round 3 opens 16 October and cl
 oses 26 November 2026\, decision 3 February 2027. Round 4 opens 27 Novembe
 r 2026 and closes 7 January 2027\, decision 9 March 2027. ROUNDS FOR THE G
 BP 40\,001-100\,000 strand: Round 1 opens 7 September and closes 1 October
  2026\, decision 30 November. Round 2 opens 23 November 2026 and closes 15
  January 2027\, decision 8 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council Engla
 nd\nLocation: England. Supports new music by living\, UK-based artists and
  music creators.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 to GBP 40\,000\, from a total annual b
 udget of GBP 3\,000\,000 for this strand in 2026/27. You must find at leas
 t 25 percent of the total project budget as CASH match funding. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Four rounds across 2026/27\; the next closes 3 Septem
 ber 2026\n\nMore: https://www.artscouncil.org.uk/music-growth-package/musi
 c-growth-fund-general-guidance?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.artscouncil.org.uk/music-growth-package/music-growth-fund-g
 eneral-guidance?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England. Supports new music by living\, UK-based artists and music
  creators.
END:VEVENT
